WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.155
Dive profile tabs, part three: reading the Gas Consumption tab.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:10.576
Click Gas Consumption and go full screen.

00:00:10.726 --> 00:00:19.481
Each line is one tank's pressure, read on the right axis: red for the twin 12s of air, dark grey for the EAN50 stage.

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:28.713
Both start full at 200 bar. The steeper the line, the faster the tank empties: about 4 bar a minute on the bottom.

00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:36.419
At 21 m you switch: the air line goes flat at 114 bar, and the stage takes over.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:47.473
The stage line flattens as you go up: about 4 bar a minute at 18 m, 2 at 6 m. A smaller tank drops faster for the same gas.

00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:56.902
The dashed line marked RESERVE is your 50 bar reserve. Both tanks stay far above it; the stage still holds over 150 bar.

00:00:57.052 --> 00:01:04.633
The green dotted line is average depth and the red dashed line maximum depth, on the left axis.

00:01:04.784 --> 00:01:13.192
This assumes a steady SAC; work, cold and stress raise it. Plan reserves by your agency's rules, such as thirds.

00:01:13.342 --> 00:01:17.056
Next: tissue loading. Thanks for watching!
